{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Pre-close audit of the acceptance criteria, done against the staged fix so the close gate is not the place these are discovered.\n\n**Status: 0 of 5 checked.** Two can be proven from the diff now; three require a real CI run and are correctly still open.\n\n**AC3 — limit unchanged, failure condition unchanged: EVIDENCE HOLDS.**\n`REBAR_CHECKOUT_PACK_LIMIT_KIB: 563200` does not appear as an added or removed line in `git diff origin/main...HEAD`, so the value is untouched. The comparison survives the step split intact: the judging step still runs `if (( SIZE_PACK_KIB > REBAR_CHECKOUT_PACK_LIMIT_KIB )); then … exit 1`. Same operator, same direction, same fail-closed exit. The only change is that the measured value now arrives through `$GITHUB_OUTPUT` as `SIZE_PACK_KIB` instead of being a shell local in the same step. The measuring step is itself fail-closed: its `awk` exits 1 if no `size-pack:` line is found, so a measurement that silently produces nothing cannot be read as zero.\n\n**AC4 — no early-warning or monitoring mechanism added: EVIDENCE HOLDS.**\nNo added line in the diff matches warn, notify, alarm, monitor, sns or cloudwatch. The change reorders and splits existing steps; it introduces no new signalling path.\n\n**AC1, AC2, AC5 — not checkable yet, by design.**\nAll three assert observed behaviour of a real run: that authorship verification executes and reports its own verdict on a run whose pack is over budget (AC1), that the pack check still fails the job on a genuine overage (AC2), and that the authorship verdict is legible without expanding a failed step (AC5). The commit has not been through CI. Checking these from the diff would be asserting an outcome rather than observing one, so they stay open until the change is green.\n\nScope note: the commit touches 4 paths, while `file_impact` still declares 1. Widening it is deliberately deferred until the change lands, because CI feedback could still alter the file set and each widening invalidates the plan attestation."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789773843029275439,"uuid":"ba6491ba-81f9-477f-b134-e66b2fb349cf"}